docs/v1.1.4/G1.1-4-LIVE-MATRIX.md
  @@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
  +**Owner constraint (restated 2026-11-13; DEC-16, 2026-10-14):** there are no separate llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama servers. All live inference goes through the homelab-ai gateway (`https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`); direct worker access is not allowed, and no separate host or GPU may be proposed. Per-kind behaviour is qualified by `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` profiles (live, over the gateway) plus the CI server-kind conformance fixtures. Any text below that says "one llama.cpp, one vLLM and one Ollama endpoint" or "the owner's llama.cpp host" is superseded by this paragraph;`eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` therefore has a gateway mode (below); the three-server mode remains for anyone who does have direct servers.
  +
   Status: **not run.** G1.1-4 (at least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported endpoints) is NOT MET until this has been run at the exact-head gate and the evidence file is committed. Nothing in this document has been executed.

   ## What it measures
  @@ -63,7 +65,14 @@ Status: **not run.** G1.1-4 (at least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supporte
  -   The llama.cpp entry is the owner's host. The matrix refuses to start unless every pinned field is present and the endpoint identifies as the configured kind.
  +   Every entry is reached through the gateway (see the owner constraint above); there is no owner llama.cpp host. The matrix refuses to start unless every pinned field is present and the endpoint identifies as the configured kind.
  +   **Gateway mode (the live configuration for this environment).** Replace `providers` with one entry per gateway model alias to be measured (at least one, no repeats, never mixed with the three direct kinds). The gateway attests neither an image nor a model digest, so those two fields are omitted (a digest that is present must still be well formed). `serverVersion` is the gateway's current `limits_version` from `/v1/models`; the run aborts before any attempt if the gateway advertises a different one. The evidence records the advertised `workers`. The key is read from the environment variable named by `apiKeyEnv`; never write the key into the file.
  +   ```json
  +   { "provider": "gateway", "serverKind": "gateway", "endpointUrl": "https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1", "apiKeyEnv": "NEXUS_GATEWAY_KEY",
  +     "serverVersion": "<limits_version>", "modelName": "<alias>", "contextSize": 8192,
  +     "sampling": { "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 1024 }, "toolChoice": "auto", "serverFlags": [], "compatibilityMode": "gateway-openai-chat" }
  +   ```
  +   Honest reading of a pass: the gateway-routed alias meets the 99.5% bar through the installed client. It is not evidence about any individual llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama build; per-kind behaviour stays with the conformance fixtures.
   5. **Run:**
      ```bash
      node eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs --config /abs/private-config.json
